# Unit state machine with retry, timeout, skip and cancel. Pending, queued and retrying units
# are also cancelled when the run stops; the full transition table is next to the diagram and in
# pipeloom.runtime.states. Illustrates section 8 (execution and scheduler) of docs/architecture.md.
...@_style
(** -> **)[*].style.font-size: 14

direction: right

pending: pending {class: process}
queued: queued {class: process}
running: running {class: process}
retrying: retrying {class: process}
succeeded: succeeded {class: store}
failed: failed {class: process}
timed_out: timed_out {class: process}
cancelled: cancelled {class: process}
skipped: skipped {class: process}

pending -> queued
queued -> running
running -> succeeded
running -> retrying: transient
retrying -> running: delay {class: meta}
running -> failed
running -> timed_out
running -> cancelled: stop
pending -> skipped: upstream failed
